A||||5||BAM-BAM||Alow me to VENT!  PLEASE!||||8||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||08-01-2000||12:57 AM||||  Ok, so they say when it rains it pours. Well, let me tell ya how true that is. I am into my third week with my suspension upgrade and every conceivable anomaly that could occur has. First of all, I digress, I haven't been working on this full time, just so you know. Here it is, KYB's, Poly's and Eibach's simple enough right. First problem was when I took the front down and realized that I had to replace the ball joints ($112.00)probably should have anyway. Then there were the first timer delays of learning as you go (Poly's went well). Next I move to the back, should be much simpler, NOT! here is where we encounter the lowering spring stock strut plunger worry. I have the old strut torn down by a proffesional and the bearing plate applied to the new KYB"S and Eibachs. This is where I learned that the two don't fit well together. They'll work ok once the car has it's weight on them, but when the wheels come off the ground for say, tire repair or replacement, Now you have to guide them back together slowly. Not to worry though a few helpfull tips from some forum members got me throught that one. Next the rear ball joints. They got torn up by the damn pickle fork (my first time) another $105.00. Ok, alls ready for the wheels to go back on and take this baby down for an alignment. Left side goes on ok, right side goes on ok, but wait, the wheels wont turn. The right side is binding up with the wheel on only. I tear the calliper out and find that the inner pad clip has broken and the inner pad is binding when the rotor tightens against it. Not a problem, get a new clip, hell while I'm at it I'll get two and replace both sides. Can't get just the clip, have to get the whole hardware kit. Ok no biggy. couldn't be that simple. The pistons are bent where the race is to accept the spring clip. rebuild kit? F*&K that, new callipers, I'm getting tierd of this sh!t. Got the new callipers ($168.00)Get the left side on no problem, right side DAMN IT! it's the wrong e-brake set up. Call for correct one, no problem; go pick it up, right box, left calliper. So I decide to change out the hardware from my old calliper to the new one with the wrong hardware. No dice, the e-brake spring base plate needs a #40 torx, got it, stripped it. I know, I'll drill it and use an easy out. Yeah right, can you guess what happened next? Let's just say that tomorrow I will get the correct calliper with the correct hardware. I'm tiered, mentally drained and completely pissed. My wife, well I'll be lucky if I have a wife after this. Well, thanks for the time. All will end well I'm sure. At least I'm sure all will end; somehow.<P>  Late, BAM (yawn) OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||8
Z||000001||Oreif||08-01-2000||02:27 AM||||I'd say your well vented now! After I redid my suspension and broke 2 bolts on the front sway bar mounts I will NEVER use "easy-outs" again. I think they were designed to break!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||08-01-2000||02:29 AM||||Damn, and I thought I had it bad because my fuel pump is startin to sound like **** ..... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Guess not....<P>But let us know how it handles when its all done, I need a suspension upgrade too.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||11
Z||000003||Formula||08-02-2000||10:43 AM||||have you ever noticed when you have some extra cash laying around the fiero breaks the right parts to use it all, but if your broke then the fiero is the most reliable car ever.<P>I learned to always say Im broke around it and it fixes a lot of problems||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||08-03-2000||02:24 AM||||I'm one set of sport/lowering springs shy of a complete suspension upgrade.  I plan on replacing all of the bolts.  I figure they'll probably break on removal anyway.  If I'm gonna spend a bunch of cash on the parts, I may as well spend an extra few dollars on new bolts.  I get frustrated easily and I'm sure I would be a little more than frustrated if one of the old bolts were to break after I installed everything new.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||08-03-2000||06:49 PM||||I don't call my car the money pit every now and then for nothing.  It acts like a Hoover vacume if you try to throw money at it to fix it.  Keep that bummed out and broke look on your face when you're around your car and don't smile too much when you hang it out on that first corner with all that new suspention under it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  That E-brake hardware, especially that damn torx bolt SUCKS.  I had to put heat to one to get it out.  The other went the way of the garbage can.  $10.00 bucks for that bolt since it doesn't come without the bracket.  shee it!||||reg||1
